fieldsmith 1
# === FIELDSMITH LITERATE CASE ===
# @id: A8
# @code: A8
# @category: analytic
# @level: Analytic Verification
# @title: Analytic Benchmark A8: Thermo-Elastic Free Expansion vs End-Clamped Uniaxial Thermal Stress (V19)
# @subtitle: Verify the two fundamental discrete Duhamel–Neumann thermo-elastic identities: (a) stress-free affine expansion u = α ΔT x under kinematic sliding supports, and (b) exact axial compressive stress σ_xx = −E α ΔT under end-clamped expansion.
# @verification_badge: Verified by V19 · Exact Duhamel–Neumann Patch Identities · PASS (0.000%)
# @doc_path: docs/analytic-tests/A8-thermoelastic-free-and-clamped-bar.md
# @fsm_path: examples/analytic/A8-thermoelastic-free-and-clamped-bar.fsm
# @starter_fsm_name: a8-thermoelastic-clamped-bar.fsm
# @verification_refs: docs/verification/V19.md
# ---
# @check: Leg (a) Free Expansion Nodal Displacement u(x) = α ΔT x & Stress || u* = α ΔT (x, y, z),   σ_ij* ≡ 0 MPa ∀ x ∈ Ω   (ΔT = 40 K) || max |u − u*| = 0 mm,  |σ| = 0 MPa || 9.98×10⁻¹² mm,  2.99×10⁻⁷ MPa || 0.000% || ≤ 10⁻⁴ mm / 0.1 MPa
# @check: Leg (b) End-Clamped Uniaxial Thermal Stress σ_xx (u_x(0) = u_x(L) = 0) || σ_xx = −E α ΔT = −70000 × (2.3×10⁻⁵) × 40 = −64.40 MPa || -64.40000 MPa || -64.40000 MPa || 0.000% || ≤ 0.1%
# @check: Leg (b) Transverse Free-Poisson Expansion u_y(y), u_z(z) & Transverse Stress || u_y = (1 + ν) α ΔT y,   u_z = (1 + ν) α ΔT z,   σ_yy = σ_zz = 0 MPa || 0.00000 MPa || -1.59×10⁻⁸ / -1.13×10⁻⁷ MPa || 0.000% || ≤ 0.1 MPa
# ---
# @assert: End-Clamped Uniaxial Thermal Stress |σ_xx| = E α ΔT || max_vm_elem || 64.4000 || 0.5% || MPa
# @assert: Uniform Nodal Temperature T = 60 °C || max_temp || 60.000 || 0.1% || °C
# ---
# @step: 1. Inspect the Kinematic Sliding + End-Clamped Supports in Setup (2) || setup
#   Open Setup (2). Fixing u_x = 0 on both ends (x = 0 and x = 40 mm) while fixing only u_y = 0 on y = 0 and u_z = 0 on z = 0 removes all 6 rigid-body modes while leaving the bar completely free to Poisson-expand laterally in Y and Z when heated from T_ref = 20 °C to T = 60 °C (ΔT = 40 K).
# @expected:
#   All six boundary faces carry T = 60 °C, and the four single-component supports eliminate rigid motion without inducing artificial transverse shear.
# @step: 2. Verify Uniform Axial Thermal Stress σ_xx = −E α ΔT in Results (3) || results
#   Switch to Results (3). Because u = (0, (1+ν)αΔT y, (1+ν)αΔT z) is affine and lies inside the P2 finite-element space, the discrete thermo-elastic solve reproduces σ_xx = −E α ΔT and σ_yy = σ_zz = 0 to 8+ significant figures.
# @expected:
#   Uniform compressive thermal stress across the entire bar with zero transverse stress.
# ---
# @theory_title: Analytic Verification A8 — Exact Discrete Thermo-Elastic Patch Test (V19)
# @theory_summary:
#   Proves that the consistent thermal load vector f_th,a = ∫_Ω B_aᵀ C α ΔT(x) dV reproduces both stress-free thermal expansion and uniaxial constrained thermal stress to machine precision on arbitrary tetrahedral meshes.
# @theory_section: A8.1 Uniaxial Constrained Thermal Expansion & Poisson Lateral Strain
# @theory_eq:
#   ε_xx = 0  ⇒  σ_xx = −E α ΔT,   σ_yy = σ_zz = 0
#   ε_yy = ε_zz = (1/E)(−ν σ_xx) + α ΔT = (1 + ν) α ΔT
# @theory_body:
#   When axial expansion is blocked (ε_xx = 0) while lateral faces are traction-free (σ_yy = σ_zz = 0), Poisson compression adds ν α ΔT to the free thermal strain α ΔT in the transverse directions, amplifying lateral expansion by (1 + ν).
# ---
# @mcp: Solve Thermo-Elastic Bar via API || solve || {"kind":"solve","dofs":25000}
#   Run the coupled conduction + thermo-elastic solver on A8.
# === END LITERATE HEADER ===

name "A8 — End-Clamped Thermo-Elastic Bar (V19)"
custommaterial alu e=70000 nu=0.33 a=2.3e-5 yield=250 density=2.7
material alu

box bar size=(40, 10, 10) at=(0, 0, 0)
region x0 = bar.nx
region x1 = bar.px
region y0 = bar.ny
region z0 = bar.nz
region all_faces = bar.nx + bar.px + bar.ny + bar.py + bar.nz + bar.pz

support fix_x0 x0 fixed=x
support fix_x1 x1 fixed=x
support fix_y0 y0 fixed=y
support fix_z0 z0 fixed=z
temperature uniform_hot all_faces temp=60 case="ClampedHot"
solve tref=20
